  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday Night through Thursday)\nIssued at 1145 PM CDT Thu Jul 23 2026\n\nThe shortwave trough axis remains over the region through Friday \nnight and into Saturday with some lingering spotty showers or\nstorms possible through the morning hours. By Saturday afternoon,\nthe shortwave will be exiting the area, with the upper ridge\nbuilding across much of the central CONUS. Heat and humidity will\nbe the story through the rest of the weekend and into at least \nthe middle part of next week. Triple digit temperatures along with higher\nhumidity will lead to heat headlines for several days. Higher \ndewpoints Saturday and Sunday could lead to some extreme heat \nwarning criteria on those days as heat indices around 115 degrees \nwill be possible. Some drier air will filter in by early next week\nbringing heat index values down somewhat, but still over advisory\nlevels for most locations through the week. Guidance is in pretty\ngood agreement that the ridge will shift west some by late week \nwith a possible frontal passage bringing temperatures back to \nnear normal and allowing low rain chances to enter back into the \nforecast.\n\nBowlan",
